The optimality condition for the primal prox-operator~\eqref{e-ls-b}
gives
\BEAS
\lefteqn{f(x^{(k+1)})-f(x)} \\
&\leq & \frac{1}{\tau_k}
  \big(d_\primal(x,x^{(k)})-d_\primal(x,x^{(k+1)})-
  d_\primal(x^{(k+1)}, x^{(k)})\big)
